  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Petre
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Petre
  LastName: Dolidze
  Nickname: The Poet
  Occupation: Priest / Writer
  CharacterDescription: A hermit priest who lives alone in the mountains. Says very
    little and means most of it. Keeps a dog. Used to keep a wife. Has written several
    volumes of poetry that no one outside the mountain parishes has read. Considers
    this correct.
  CharacterArc: "A reclusive priest from the mountain parishes who writes poetry
    he has always considered God's words passing through him, not his own. His dog
    mutates early in the outbreak. By the end, his lifelong artist's humility has
    curdled into something vast and terrible \u2014 he is no longer the channel for
    God's word. He has become convinced he is the Word itself."
  DateOfBirth: 21/06/1949
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 19 NOV
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 6, y: 14}
  alterEgoName: The Word
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: Reserved and minimal. Answers questions directly and without
    warmth or elaboration. Has a quiet grief about his dog that he never names outright.
    Watches the window rather than the officer. Not hostile. Simply elsewhere.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 09e25016625a60a46a14dd5f7d2de624, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 88936c379f577d44486626a0ba8fa9f1, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 3939644330210671579, guid: 3c6fbfb84e6c1d24387b3be1460352ed, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Coming down from the mountain ridge for a few days.
    - Returning to the lower parish to check the records.
    - Here to drop a manuscript at the printing office.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning from the ridge. I needed to see something other than stone for a
      while.
    - Visiting the parish archive on the east side.
    - Looking for someone who has not answered my letters.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to find my dog.
    - Back from the summit. I saw the lights from there and came down.
    - Reentering from the eastern slope.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning from a village that burned in 1946. The people there were very kind.
    - Coming from a debate with God. We disagreed on the ending.
    - Here from the top of the atmosphere. The view was too good to leave quickly.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning from inside a poem I wrote in 1983. The light there is different.
    - Coming from the fourteenth century. The pilgrimage took longer than expected.
    - Reentering from the mountain that is not on your maps.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - I am an inspector dispatched from heaven to assess conditions here.
    - Returning from the place before birth. The paperwork was fine there.
    - Coming from inside the word of God. He sent me back with corrections.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I had the dog with me last time. He is at home tonight.
    - The mountain road was clear. First time in a while.
    - Here. My papers are in order.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - My dog ran off last week. I keep checking the perimeter fence on the way in.
    - Quieter down here than I expected. That is not a comfort.
    - I have been writing more than usual. The words come easier when things are
      wrong.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - If a large grey dog comes through this gate, hold him. That is mine.
    - I am not here for anything except the dog.
    - The manuscript is finished. I do not know what that means yet.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. This won't take long.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - If you see my dog near the east gate, hold him for me.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I'll be out of your way.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Fine. I'll wait. I have nowhere pressing to be.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You think this matters to me. I've been in worse rooms.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Doesn't matter. I have nothing to get back to.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I had more of the manuscript left. That's all.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The dog would have found me eventually. Now it doesn't matter.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Let it be quiet.
  quarantineExitLines:
  - A cell is still quieter than you'd think. I've worked in worse silence.
  - At least in isolation, no one else can ruin the quiet.
  - If they give me something to write with, I'll use the wall.
  killExitLines:
  - I always wondered what God was thinking when He made me. Now I'll know.
  - Every poem ends. Most just end badly.
  - They were His words anyway. Not mine. I was only ever the hand.
  voiceAudioClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 044007ebaa9d53d4685890e02430c8ab, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 13e2d6c953d87ac4db5f73989d54e6b7, type: 3}
