  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1714e5de92f12ae479cbbdd6d7866c18, type: 3}
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2b51582647a3f8340ac72eb350384322, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The ridge path above the northern district. I walk at dusk when
      I can.
    midDaysAnswer: Nowhere specific. I had to leave the mountain for a while.
    finalDaysAnswer: The eastern slope. I was looking for something.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I have not left in days. I don't walk the ridge
      at night. I never do that.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The chapel. A meeting. Several of us. Very ordinary gathering.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Inside. I have been inside this whole time. Not near
      the slope at all.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I sleep poorly but that has always been the case.
    midDaysAnswer: I have been hearing things at night. Probably the wind through
      the pass.
    finalDaysAnswer: My hands don't shake but something in them wants to. I write
      through it.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing at all. Very clear head. The clearest I've had
      in years. I sleep excellently.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: I hear nothing unusual. The nights are very quiet. I have
      no complaints.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My hands are perfectly still. I am a very calm person.
      I have always been calm.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No one. I have my dog.
    midDaysAnswer: Just myself now. My dog ran off last week.
    finalDaysAnswer: Alone. Completely.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No one. Always alone. I don't have a dog. I've never
      had a dog.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My family. A large family. A full house. Very warm.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My dog. Right at my heels. He is waiting outside the
      gate right now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I had the dog with me last time. He is at home tonight.
    - I write when I cannot sleep. Lately I cannot sleep very much.
    - Quiet suits me. I don't say that as a complaint.
    midDays:
    - My dog has been gone for nearly two weeks. I don't know where he went.
    - I have been writing more than usual. There is nothing else to do in the quiet.
    - The mountain has changed. Something about the way it sits now.
    finalDays:
    - If you see a large grey dog near the perimeter fence, that is mine. He would
      not have gone far on his own.
    - I have been leaving food outside the east gate. He has not come.
    - The words don't come from me. They never did. I was only ever the hand holding
      the pen.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 4819203
